### 5. Recommendation & AI Core Algorithms
Sloth adapts open-source implementations and formulations from the following peer-reviewed works:
- **LightHGCN**:
  - *Source*: "LightGCN: Simplifying and Powering Graph Convolution Network for Recommendation", Xiangnan He et al. (SIGIR 2020)
  - *Reference*: https://github.com/gusye1234/LightGCN-PyTorch (MIT)
  - *Target*: `server/engine/graph/light_hgcn.py` (5-node heterogeneous hypergraph convolution)
- **BERT4Rec**:
  - *Source*: "BERT4Rec: Sequential Recommendation with Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformer", Fei Sun et al. (CIKM 2019)
  - *Reference*: https://github.com/jaywonchung/BERT4Rec-VAE-Pytorch (MIT)
  - *Target*: `server/engine/sequential/bert4rec.py` (Bidirectional Transformer sequential recommender)
- **ACT-R Cognitive Memory Decay**:
  - *Source*: "Transformers Meet ACT-R: Repeat-Aware and Sequential Listening Session Recommendation", Viet-Anh Tran et al. (ACM RecSys 2024 / Deezer Research)
  - *Reference*: https://github.com/deezer/recsys24-pisa (MIT)
  - *Target*: `server/engine/sequential/actr_memory.py` (Base-level activation decay, spreading activation, partial matching)
- **DiffRec / L-DiffRec**:
  - *Source*: "Diffusion Recommender Model", Yiyan Xu et al. (SIGIR 2023)
  - *Reference*: https://github.com/YiyanXu/DiffRec (MIT)
  - *Target*: `server/engine/generator/playlist_diffusion.py` (Latent diffusion playlist generation in MERT space)
- **IPS Debiasing**:
  - *Source*: "Recommendations as Treatments: Debiasing Learning and Evaluation", Tobias Schnabel et al. (ICML 2016)
  - *Reference*: https://github.com/jiawei-chen/RecDebiasing (MIT)
  - *Target*: `server/engine/coldstart/ips_debiasing.py` (Inverse propensity scoring derived from SQLite play_count)
- **Thompson Sampling Bandit**:
  - *Source*: "Analysis of Thompson Sampling for the Multi-armed Bandit Problem", Shipra Agrawal & Navin Goyal (COLT 2012)
  - *Target*: `server/engine/coldstart/thompson_bandit.py` (Beta-Bernoulli bandit for cold start exploration/exploitation)
- **MERT**:
  - *Source*: "MERT: Acoustic Music Understanding Model with Large-Scale Self-supervised Training", Yizhi Li et al. (ICLR 2024)
  - *Reference*: https://github.com/yizhilll/MERT (Apache-2.0)
  - *Target*: `server/engine/audio/mert_extractor.py` (24kHz audio hidden state extraction to 768-dim embeddings)
- **CLAP**:
  - *Source*: "Large-Scale Contrastive Language-Audio Pretraining with Feature Fusion and Keyword-to-Caption Augmentation", Yusong Wu et al. (ICASSP 2023)
  - *Reference*: https://github.com/LAION-AI/CLAP (MIT)
  - *Target*: `server/engine/audio/clap_extractor.py` (48kHz audio and text joint multimodal embedding for semantic search)

